+# Exploratory source-unit and fit-usage comparison
+
+This comparison was formulated after reading the report's 226MPa C65 labels, Table6 repeated room-temperature measurements and lm definition. It is exploratory, not blind/preregistered confirmation of a baseline rule. Preserve the exact CSV and report records.
+
+Compute room-temperature groups within This study using exact specimen strings and T=20, with original FY20/RFy/FY002 values retained. Report counts, unique RFy/FY20 values and descriptive mean strengths; no mean is declared the authors' intended denominator. For C65_FL, compare all room-temperature rows and separate strain-rate groups; both scopes are retained without selecting the one that best matches226.
+
+Transcribe the selected source Table6 tuple from physical38/printed36: C65,T20,rate8.75e-5,S002264MPa,S02370MPa,Su469MPa,Elt38,RA63.1,lm0. Seek candidate CSV counterparts under the explicit tentative C65→C65_FL cross-reference and sameT/rate, with yield-strength difference at most0.5MPa and the other listed values exact. This is a numeric candidate join under an assumed rounding interval, not authenticated coupon/negative/physical custody. Preserve263.5and264separately and report all matches.
+
+Compare the Figure2 literal caption rate interval3.30e-5<rate<1.35e-4 against the68Thisstudyrows only to show that a complete CSV population is not automatically a figure-specific input set. The body also says within or just slightly outside standard ranges; do not convert that undefined allowance into a selected filter. No model or figure fit is rerun.
+
+Inspect Figure2 for the qualitative source observation that green Thisstudy points at its near-room-temperature end appear above and below R=1. Do not digitize values, assign a particular point to a coupon, claim independent calibration or equate the figure population with every currentCSVrow. Retain this observation beside any all-unity CSV room-temperature values as a figure/export relationship question.
+
+The lm0 flag denotes non-use in computing Eq10 stress–strain parameters. It does not establish exclusion from retained-strength, Figure2, another model or the2005collapse analysis. The original CSV has no lm field; missing encoding is not proof of missing analysis. All preceding fields and uncertainty remain unchanged.
